description.narrative:
Output: Quality and relevance of secondary education improved Indicator: Project 1c. Grade 11 students in STEM schools meeting acceptable standards on NAM increased by 5% (results disaggregated by sex and further by ethnicity).
(Baseline: mathematics 54.9% in SY2012). Progress/Status: NAM 2021-2022 was held in April 2022. Data is available in December 2022 and the National Report will be published in June 2023;
Data on grade 11 students&apos; achievement (of the subject of Literature, Maths, English) at project&apos;s beneficiary schools and other schools across the country have been collected. Data Source: Center of Education Quality Assurance, MOET annual evaluation of student competencies of the new curriculum as measured by grade 11 NAM results in STEM and control group schools. Actual value:

